text:
maria: Heads-up — BigBank wants us to run an SDK integration for streaming + function/tool calls that returns structured transaction summaries with PII redaction. They require EU data residency, KMS, and a security questionnaire answered. Need a presales canary runbook, a lightweight pricing sketch for Dedicated vs Hosted fallback, and a test plan for 200 qps bursty traffic. Can someone pair on this?

devon: I can own the runbook. Quick clarifying q's: do they want partial/streaming partial results (low latency) or fully assembled JSON at the end? And will the model invoke external webhooks (tool-calls) for redaction, or should model emit redaction hints for us to post-process?

maria: They want streaming partial tokens for UX, and model-initiated function/tool calls to our redact webhook when PII is detected. Schema validation is required (we'll enforce JSON contract). Timeline 2 weeks for an initial canary.

anil: Pricing sketch notes: Hosted — per-token + streaming surcharge; Dedicated — monthly reserved GPU SKU with lower per-token runtime cost. Need expected tokens/session and concurrency to give a concrete SKU. For canary, recommend 1k synthetic sessions across EU region to validate latency & correctness. I'll draft a delta table for cross-region egress and fallback routing.

lee: Security checklist: for Private/Dedicated we can enable customer-managed KMS + VPC endpoints and mTLS to the webhook. For Hosted we can offer region pinning (eu-west-1) and encryption-at-rest; SOC2 + PCI considerations should be addressed separately. For canary use synthetic PII, disable persistent request logs, and capture only schema validation metrics.

devon: Minimal SDK streaming example & structured output contract below — drop into runbook.

```js
// streaming + onFunctionCall example (pseudo)
const stream = await RedwoodSDK.stream({
  model: 'redwood-turbo-1',
  streaming: true,
  onFunctionCall: async (fn) => {
    // call our redact service
    await fetch('https://redact.example.com/call', {
      method: 'POST',
      body: JSON.stringify(fn.arguments),
      headers: { 'Authorization': 'Bearer <secrets>' }
    });
  }
});
stream.on('data', chunk => render(chunk));
```

Structured output schema (stringified JSON example):
```json
{"transaction_summary": {"transaction_id": "txn_12345", "amount_usd": 123.45, "merchant": "ACME Corp", "timestamp": "2025-11-30T12:34:56Z", "redaction": "PII_REDACTED", "flags": ["suspicious_amount"]}}
```

maria: Nice. For fallback, can we automatically route to a hosted-compatible quantized variant if Dedicated capacity is saturated, and still preserve function-call compatibility? We need contract tests so schema doesn't drift.

anil: Yes — we can configure policy: prefer dedicated model v1, fallback to hosted v1-quantized. We'll add model-contract tests that validate schema and example prompts. I'll include a pricing delta for fallback egress + additional per-minute routing charges.

ci-bot: deploy-bot: Canary job scheduled: 2025-12-01T03:00:00Z UTC — will run synthetic sessions and schema validation.

lee: I'll prepare the runbook + checklist items: KMS key rotation, VPC peering steps, allowed IP ranges, certificate distribution, test harness instructions, and a loadgen script. Also will add instructions to disable persistent logs for canary traffic. Ping me for env access.

maria: Thanks — action items: devon to drop runbook draft by EOD Friday; anil to provide pricing SKU sketch by Monday; lee to add runbook checklist and loadgen; i'll confirm EU residency acceptance and risk items with BigBank. If anyone else wants to pair on the canary, DM me. :thumbsup:
